 "conclusion": "ZERO full-InChIKey and ZERO skeleton-InChIKey overlap in either pool: none of the five enumerable lipidoids is already in the corpus. But the NEAR MISS is the important result. The corpus already carries 173 unique structures over 277 in-vitro rows (11 experiments) and 25 in-vivo rows (4) built on this exact amine head, named 93_O12 / 93_O14 / 93_N12 by AA_2008 and A93_C12 by KW_2014. Those are two independent curations of two unrelated papers, and together with curation/xuq_32520527 (which read head 93 off a drawn figure in a third paper) they fix amine 93 = 1-(3-aminopropyl)imidazole from three sources this paper did not supply. They also confirm this paper's tail-prefix convention externally: AA_2008 carries 93_O14 as a tetradecyl ESTER and 93_N14 as the corresponding AMIDE on the same head, which is exactly the O/N split the SI's O16S-S / N16S-S pair implies. REPORTED, NOT ACTED ON."
